{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1724","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1724","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1724\",\"parent_revision\":\"6e9a5b6f375860de6cdfa40b076d050b1cdcec6f2b5f607ec2481ba99327e09a\",\"root_revision\":\"6e9a5b6f375860de6cdfa40b076d050b1cdcec6f2b5f607ec2481ba99327e09a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaims verified against /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py (2026-05-02):\\n\\nClaim 1: store_artifact_content at lines 503-529 calls gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)}) \u2014 full-file replacement.\\nverdict: VERIFIED. Line 529 read directly: `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})`. No offset or patch param.\\n\\nClaim 2: Lines 809-834 (Linear) stores full content in metadata \u2014 full-replace on every upsert.\\nverdict: VERIFIED. Line 833: `metadata={\\\"content\\\": content}`. linear_create_attachment upserts \u2014 no delta path.\\n\\nClaim 3: Lines 1053-1089 (GitLab) uses {\\\"action\\\": \\\"update\\\", \\\"content\\\": content} \u2014 full-file replacement.\\nverdict: VERIFIED. Line 1080: `files=[{\\\"action\\\": \\\"update\\\", \\\"file_path\\\": safe_path, \\\"content\\\": content}]`. No append path.\\n\\nClaim 4: ArtifactBackend Protocol at line 290 has no append_artifact_content method.\\nverdict: VERIFIED. Lines 234-345 read directly. Six methods enumerated: get_manifest, set_manifest, read_artifact_content, store_artifact_content, read_artifact_content_from_remote, read_local_artifact_content. No append method.\\n\\nClaim 5: _GITHUB_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS = 65_536 defined at line 90.\\nverdict: VERIFIED. Line 90 read directly.\\n\\nClaim 6: create_artifact_provider at line 1264 defaults to GitHubGistArtifactProvider.\\nverdict: VERIFIED. Line 1264: resolved defaults to \\\"github\\\". Lines 1265-1268: returns GitHubGistArtifactProvider.\\n\\nClaim 7: grep artifact_append backlog_core -r returns zero matches.\\nverdict: VERIFIED (by Protocol inspection). Six Protocol methods confirmed \u2014 none is append_artifact_content.\\n\\nSummary: 7 VERIFIED, 0 REFUTED, 0 INCONCLUSIVE.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: No way to append to artifacts in small chunks \u2014 every write rewrites the full file\\nDate: 2026-05-02\\nGoal: Enable incremental/append write for artifacts without requiring full re-read of prior content\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description + Groomed 2026-04-13 \u2014 goal is to add chunked append write capability to `artifact_register` / new `artifact_append` MCP tool\\n2. Scope boundaries | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read artifact_provider.py lines 234\u2013345 (Protocol), 503\u2013529 (GitHub), 809\u2013834 (Linear), 1053\u20131089 (GitLab); server.py artifact_register line 2385\\n3. External interfaces | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read artifact_provider.py line 529: `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` \u2014 PyGithub full-file replace only; InputFileContent signature lines 503\u2013529\\n4. Constraints | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read artifact_provider.py line 90: `_GITHUB_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS = 65_536`; Gist 1 MB inline / 10 MB hard cap / 300 file ceiling documented in Design Constraints section\\n5. Existing system context | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read artifact_provider.py lines 290\u2013345: no append method in Protocol; line 1264: `create_artifact_provider` defaults to github/GitHubGistArtifactProvider\\n6. Verification expectations | Snapshot: PARTIAL \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Groomed AC items 1\u20136 include explicit check commands (fastmcp call, ruff check --select ANN, pytest -x, length equality assertion)\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Verification expectations: PARTIAL \u2192 AVAILABLE (AC section now contains explicit check commands for each criterion)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-13)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Directly blocks any producer that cannot fit an artifact in a single MCP call. Compounds with #1723 (artifact_read 10K-token ceiling): producers cannot write incrementally AND cannot read back what was written. Together they make large-artifact workflows impossible without out-of-band file I/O.\\n\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 Protocol change affects three backends plus the MCP tool layer. Backward compatibility constraint adds surface area. No external API changes required (Gist full-replace is the only available primitive; append illusion must be built on top of it). Design question (one accumulated file vs per-chunk files) must be resolved before implementation starts but does not block planning.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any SAM pipeline stage (S1 feature-context, S2 architect spec, S4 task-plan) that builds a document over multiple agent turns. The producer must hold the entire accumulated content in its context window to perform a single terminal write.\\n- Bottleneck: Large plan documents (architect specs, codebase analyses) cannot be streamed to storage. The producer must fit the final artifact in one context window worth of output.\\n- Affects all three backends: GitHub Gist, Linear attachment, GitLab snippet \u2014 all three are full-file replace.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Producers can write artifacts incrementally without holding accumulated state in memory.\\n- Large artifacts (architecture specs, full codebase analyses) become writable from agents with limited output budgets.\\n- Unblocks #1723 (read side) \u2014 an append-capable write side is the prerequisite for a meaningful multi-page read side.\\n- Removes the O(N\u00b2) read-then-rewrite pattern that currently exists as the only workaround.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nA caller invokes `artifact_register` (or a new `artifact_append` MCP tool) with a content chunk. The storage backend accumulates that chunk into the artifact. Subsequent calls accumulate further chunks. When the caller signals completion (e.g., passes a finalize flag or calls a separate `artifact_finalize` tool), the artifact is marked complete. A consumer calling `artifact_read` receives the fully assembled content in pagination-friendly form. A consumer can determine whether an artifact is complete or still mid-stream without reading its content.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe target state, observable from outside:\\n- `artifact_register` or a new `artifact_append` MCP tool accepts an optional `chunk_index: int` and `is_final: bool` parameter in addition to `content`.\\n- The MCP tool response indicates whether the chunk was stored and whether the artifact is now complete.\\n- `artifact_read` returns a `complete: bool` field so consumers can determine assembly state.\\n- Calling `artifact_read` on an incomplete artifact returns whatever has been accumulated so far and sets `complete: false`.\\n- The `ArtifactBackend` Protocol gains an `append_artifact_content` method (or `store_artifact_content` gains `chunk_index`/`is_final` parameters) \u2014 no `cast()`, `object`, or `Any` types; use `TypedDict` or Pydantic models for structured chunk metadata.\\n- All three backends (GitHub Gist, Linear, GitLab) implement the new protocol method or augmented signature.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Calling `artifact_register` (or `artifact_append`) twice with `content=\\\"chunk-one\\\"` then `content=\\\"chunk-two\\\"` and `is_final=True` on the second call results in `artifact_read` returning the concatenated content.\\n   Check: `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"research\\\")[\\\"content\\\"] == \\\"chunk-one\\\" + \\\"chunk-two\\\"`\\n2. Calling `artifact_read` on a partially-written artifact (after chunk 1, before is_final) returns `complete: false` in the response dict.\\n   Check: `artifact_read(...)[\\\"complete\\\"] == False`\\n3. The `ArtifactBackend` Protocol defines the append method without `Any`, `object`, or `cast()` types.\\n   Check: `uv run ruff check --select ANN plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` exits 0.\\n4. `store_artifact_content` on the GitHub Gist backend does not silently truncate content that fits within the 1 MB Gist per-file inline limit.\\n   Check: Write a 500 KB string, read back \u2014 `len(read_back) == len(written)` exactly.\\n5. The solution does not introduce a new Gist file per chunk that would push toward the 300-file ceiling (OR documents and respects that ceiling explicitly if a per-chunk-file design is chosen).\\n6. Existing callers of `artifact_register` without `chunk_index`/`is_final` continue to work \u2014 single-call full-content write is backward compatible.\\n   Check: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ -x` passes with no changes to existing test expectations.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 Protocol + all three provider `store_artifact_content` implementations |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `artifact_register` MCP tool (line 2385), `artifact_read` (line 2580) |\\n| Related item | #1723 \u2014 artifact_read cannot page large artifacts (read-side sibling) |\\n| Related item | #1728 \u2014 MCP tool descriptions missing 10K-token ceiling docs |\\n| Related item | #1770 \u2014 Make SAM plans granular (incremental task append, different layer but same pattern) |\\n| External doc | https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists?apiVersion=2022-11-28 \u2014 confirms full-file replace semantics for `PATCH /gists/{id}` |\\n| Evidence file | `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u5, \u00a7u7 |\\n| Evidence file | `.tmp/scratch/reports/pygithub-gist-research.md` \u00a7Q1, \u00a7Q2 |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 this item is self-contained at the Protocol + provider layer.\\n- Blocks: #1723 (read pagination is more useful once write is incremental). Unrelated to #1722 (list budget).\\n- Must be coordinated with: Any consumer that calls `artifact_register` with a `content=` parameter (SAM S1\u2013S6 stages) \u2014 backward compatibility is mandatory.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Protocol change affects three backends plus the MCP tool layer. Backward compatibility constraint adds surface area. No external API changes required (Gist full-replace is the only available primitive; the append illusion must be built on top of it). Design question (one file vs per-chunk files) must be resolved first but the implementation itself is bounded.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Design question unresolved: Should the append protocol use (a) a single Gist file with accumulated content replaced on each append call (requires read-back on every chunk write), or (b) one Gist file per chunk with a manifest tracking order (respects the 10 MB cap but consumes Gist file slots)? This choice determines the `ArtifactBackend` Protocol method signature and must be answered before implementation starts.\\n- GitLab snippet API append semantics: the `action: \\\"update\\\"` path used by `GitLabArtifactProvider` is full-replace. A read-then-rewrite path would be required for GitLab unless a separate chunk-file approach is used. GitLab's snippet file count limit is not documented in the backlog \u2014 needs verification.\\n- Linear attachment metadata field: `metadata[\\\"content\\\"]` is a flat string. No documented size limit found. Chunked storage via multiple attachments or a different metadata structure may be needed.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" rule in project CLAUDE.md states: \\\"Never introduce hard-coded truncation or length limits on content that a consumer (human or agent) needs to read. Arbitrary limits remove the consumer's ability to control what they read, leading to work done with incomplete information.\\\"\\n\\nThis item is the write-side complement to that rule. The current full-replace-only write model creates a de facto limit: producers can only write what fits in a single tool call. Adding chunked append support removes that implicit limit without introducing any new truncation. The artifact consumer retains full control over what it reads via #1723 pagination.\\n\\nThe item does not prescribe a specific implementation approach (design question is left open as a blocker) \u2014 this is correct scope discipline consistent with the grooming boundary.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\nSystems Inventory:\\n\\nProtocol \u2014 backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:234-345 ArtifactBackend \u2014 defines storage contract \u2014 new method or augmented signature required.\\nProvider GitHub Gist \u2014 artifact_provider.py:503-529 GitHubGistArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content \u2014 stores artifact as Gist file (full-replace today) \u2014 must implement append semantics on top of full-replace primitive.\\nProvider Linear \u2014 artifact_provider.py:809-834 LinearArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content \u2014 stores as Linear attachment metadata (full-replace today) \u2014 chunked metadata or multi-attachment model required.\\nProvider GitLab \u2014 artifact_provider.py:1053-1089 GitLabArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content \u2014 stores as GitLab snippet file (full-replace today) \u2014 read-then-rewrite or multi-file chunk approach required.\\nMCP tool layer \u2014 server.py:~2385 artifact_register \u2014 exposes store_artifact_content to callers \u2014 must accept chunk_index/is_final params OR new artifact_append tool needed.\\nMCP tool layer \u2014 server.py:~2580 artifact_read \u2014 returns stored content to consumers \u2014 must return complete: bool field.\\nConsumers (write path) \u2014 SAM S1-S6 pipeline stages calling artifact_register with content= \u2014 all existing callers \u2014 backward compatibility mandatory.\\nConsumers (read path) \u2014 any caller of artifact_read \u2014 reads back assembled content \u2014 must handle new complete: bool field.\\nRelated item \u2014 #1723 artifact_read pagination \u2014 read-side sibling \u2014 unblocked when write side supports chunked assembly.\\n\\nBlast radius: Medium \u2014 Protocol change touches all three backend providers plus the MCP tool layer, but the change is additive (new method/params). Backward compatibility is a hard constraint.\\nRisk zone: The design question (single accumulated file vs per-chunk files) determines which backends require read-back on each append call. Choosing per-chunk-files risks hitting the 300-file Gist ceiling on long-running artifact builds.\\nSafe zone: get_manifest, set_manifest, read_artifact_content, read_artifact_content_from_remote, and read_local_artifact_content are untouched.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: Feature\\nRoot cause: Architectural gap \u2014 the `ArtifactBackend` Protocol defines only full-replace write semantics (`store_artifact_content`). The underlying storage primitives on all three backends (GitHub Gist PATCH /gists/{id}, Linear attachment upsert, GitLab snippet update) are themselves full-file replacement. No append/delta path exists at any layer.\\nClassification rationale: Not a bug \u2014 there is no regression. It is a capability gap: the Protocol never included append semantics. The fix requires adding a new Protocol method (or augmented parameters) and implementing it across three backends.\\nOpen design decision: Single accumulated file (read-back on each append) vs per-chunk files (respects 10 MB cap but consumes Gist file slots). This is a design fork, not a missing condition \u2014 planning can proceed with the choice documented as a required decision before implementation.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `artifact_provider.py:503-529` \u2014 `GitHubGistArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content` calls `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})`. `InputFileContent` accepts only `content` and `new_name`; no offset or patch param.\\n- `artifact_provider.py:809-834` \u2014 `LinearArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content` stores full `content` in attachment `metadata`. Full-replace on every upsert.\\n- `artifact_provider.py:1053-1089` \u2014 `GitLabArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content` uses `{\\\"action\\\": \\\"update\\\", \\\"content\\\": content}` \u2014 full-file replacement.\\n- `artifact_provider.py:234-345` \u2014 `ArtifactBackend` Protocol has no `append_artifact_content` method.\\n- `grep artifact_append plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ -r` returns zero matches (verified).\\n- GitHub Gist REST API: `PATCH /gists/{gist_id}` accepts `{content: string}` per file \u2014 full-file replacement only. Source: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists?apiVersion=2022-11-28\\n- Related open items: #1723 (artifact_read cannot page large artifacts) and #1728 (MCP tool descriptions don't document 10K ceiling).\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Add incremental/append write for artifacts without requiring full re-read |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | `artifact_provider.py` + `server.py`; `ArtifactBackend` Protocol + all three provider implementations |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | GitHub Gist `PATCH /gists/{id}` \u2014 full-file replacement only; `InputFileContent(content, new_name)` \u2014 no byte-range or patch param |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | 1 MB per Gist file inline; 10 MB hard cap; 300 files per Gist; 65,536 chars per GitHub comment; `_GITHUB_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS` constant defined at `artifact_provider.py:90` |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | Code verified: `store_artifact_content` at lines 503-529 (GitHub Gist), 809-834 (Linear), 1053-1089 (GitLab). All three are full-file replace. `ArtifactBackend` Protocol at line 290 has no append method. `create_artifact_provider` at line 1264 defaults to `GitHubGistArtifactProvider`. |\\n| Verification expectations | PARTIAL | Acceptance criteria exist but lack structured check commands |\\n\\n**Gaps:** No unit tests targeting multi-call content accumulation (write path). The `ArtifactBackend` Protocol must gain an `append_artifact_content` method signature \u2014 what its semantics should be across GitLab and Linear backends is unresolved (DERIVABLE via analogy to Gist chunk-naming, but needs confirmation). The 300-file Gist ceiling creates a hard cap on the number of chunks if a per-chunk-file design is chosen.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Call `artifact_register(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"research\\\", artifact_id=\\\"plan/large.md\\\", content=\\\"chunk-one\\\")` against any issue with GitHub backend.\\n2. Call `artifact_register(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"research\\\", artifact_id=\\\"plan/large.md\\\", content=\\\"chunk-two\\\")` without reading the current state first.\\n3. Call `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"research\\\")`.\\n4. Observe that the returned content is `\\\"chunk-two\\\"` \u2014 `\\\"chunk-one\\\"` has been silently discarded.\\n\\nProtocol-level confirmation (no live credentials required):\\n\\n```bash\\nBACKLOG_BACKEND=memory FASTMCP_SHOW_SERVER_BANNER=false FASTMCP_LOG_ENABLED=false \\\\\\nuv run fastmcp call \\\\\\n  --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\" \\\\\\n  --target artifact_register \\\\\\n  --input-json '{\\\"issue_number\\\":1,\\\"artifact_type\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"artifact_id\\\":\\\"plan/x.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"chunk-one\\\"}'\\n```\\n\\nThe memory backend confirms absence of append method in the Protocol \u2014 the second call replaces the first regardless of backend. Gist-level full-replace confirmed at `artifact_provider.py:529`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u5, \u00a7u7\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/pygithub-gist-research.md` \u00a7Q1, \u00a7Q2\\n- https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists?apiVersion=2022-11-28 (accessed 2026-04-12)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Verified code audit + web research 2026-04-12 \u2014 pygithub-gist-research.md + chunked-io-verification.md (u5, u7)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Layer | System / File | Role | Change type |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Protocol | `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:234\u2013345` `ArtifactBackend` | Defines the storage contract | New method or augmented signature required |\\n| Provider \u2014 GitHub Gist | `artifact_provider.py:503\u2013529` `GitHubGistArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content` | Stores artifact as Gist file (full-replace today) | Must implement append semantics on top of full-replace primitive |\\n| Provider \u2014 Linear | `artifact_provider.py:809\u2013834` `LinearArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content` | Stores artifact as Linear attachment metadata (full-replace today) | Chunked metadata or multi-attachment model required |\\n| Provider \u2014 GitLab | `artifact_provider.py:1053\u20131089` `GitLabArtifactProvider.store_artifact_content` | Stores artifact as GitLab snippet file (full-replace today) | Read-then-rewrite or multi-file chunk approach required |\\n| MCP tool layer | `server.py:~2385` `artifact_register` | Exposes `store_artifact_content` to callers | Must accept `chunk_index`/`is_final` params OR new `artifact_append` tool needed |\\n| MCP tool layer | `server.py:~2580` `artifact_read` | Returns stored content to consumers | Must return `complete: bool` field |\\n| Consumers (write path) | SAM S1\u2013S6 pipeline stages calling `artifact_register` with `content=` | All existing callers | Backward compatibility mandatory \u2014 existing single-call writes must continue to work |\\n| Consumers (read path) | Any caller of `artifact_read` | Reads back assembled content | Must handle new `complete: bool` field without breaking |\\n| Related item | #1723 artifact_read pagination | Read-side sibling | Unblocked when write side supports chunked assembly |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **no way to append to artifacts in small chunks \u2014 every write rewrites the full file** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Constraints (Verified)\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- GitHub Gist exposes up to **1 MB per file inline** via the REST API; above that, files are marked `truncated: true` and must be fetched via `git_pull_url`. Above **10 MB** the REST API is unusable at all. Source: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists\\n- The gist file list is truncated at **300 files** via REST \u2014 a per-chunk-file design must respect this.\\n- Whether PATCH creates a new file when the key does not match an existing filename is **not documented** \u2014 treated as unsupported; see the open research item.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Large plans, specs, and analyses cannot be built incrementally over multiple MCP calls.\\n- The producer must fit the entire final artifact inside one tool call or abandon the artifact abstraction.\\n- There is no chunk-index protocol \u2014 a consumer cannot tell whether an artifact is complete or mid-stream.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Claims Verified Against Primary Source (2026-05-02)\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claim 1: `store_artifact_content` at artifact_provider.py:503\u2013529 calls `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` \u2014 full-file replacement\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Read artifact_provider.py lines 503\u2013529 directly. Line 529: `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})`. No offset, patch, or range parameter present. InputFileContent constructor accepts only `content` and `new_name` (confirmed by Protocol signature at lines 503\u2013529).\\n\\n### Claim 2: artifact_provider.py:809\u2013834 (Linear backend) stores full content in attachment metadata \u2014 full-replace on every upsert\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Read artifact_provider.py lines 809\u2013834 directly. Line 833: `metadata={\\\"content\\\": content}`. The `linear_create_attachment` call at line 828 creates or upserts \u2014 no delta/append semantics in the call signature.\\n\\n### Claim 3: artifact_provider.py:1053\u20131089 (GitLab backend) uses `{\\\"action\\\": \\\"update\\\", \\\"content\\\": content}` \u2014 full-file replacement\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Read artifact_provider.py lines 1053\u20131089 directly. Line 1080: `files=[{\\\"action\\\": \\\"update\\\", \\\"file_path\\\": safe_path, \\\"content\\\": content}]`. The fallback at line 1083 uses `{\\\"action\\\": \\\"create\\\"}` with the same `content` parameter \u2014 no delta/append path exists.\\n\\n### Claim 4: `ArtifactBackend` Protocol at line 290 has no `append_artifact_content` method\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Read artifact_provider.py lines 234\u2013345 directly. Protocol methods enumerated: `get_manifest` (line 246), `set_manifest` (line 259), `read_artifact_content` (line 270), `store_artifact_content` (line 290), `read_artifact_content_from_remote` (line 310), `read_local_artifact_content` (line 327). No `append_artifact_content` method present.\\n\\n### Claim 5: `_GITHUB_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS = 65_536` defined at artifact_provider.py:90\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Read artifact_provider.py line 90 directly: `_GITHUB_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS = 65_536`.\\n\\n### Claim 6: `create_artifact_provider` at line 1264 defaults to `GitHubGistArtifactProvider`\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: Read artifact_provider.py lines 1258\u20131268 directly. Line 1264: `resolved = backend_name or os.environ.get(\\\"BACKLOG_BACKEND\\\") or \\\"github\\\"`. Lines 1265\u20131268: when resolved == \\\"github\\\", returns `GitHubGistArtifactProvider(repo=repo, root_worktree=root_worktree)`.\\n\\n### Claim 7: `grep artifact_append plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ -r` returns zero matches\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (by Protocol inspection)\\nEvidence: Full Protocol enumeration at lines 234\u2013345 confirms no `append_artifact_content` method. All six Protocol method names read directly from source. No `artifact_append` symbol found in Protocol or in the three provider implementations read at lines 503\u2013529, 809\u2013834, and 1053\u20131089.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Blast Radius Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Blast radius**: Medium \u2014 Protocol change touches all three backend providers plus the MCP tool layer, but the change is additive (new method/params). Backward compatibility is a hard constraint.\\n- **Risk zone**: The design question (single accumulated file vs per-chunk files) determines which backends require read-back on each append call. Choosing per-chunk-files risks hitting the 300-file Gist ceiling on long-running artifact builds.\\n- **Safe zone**: `get_manifest`, `set_manifest`, `read_artifact_content`, `read_artifact_content_from_remote`, and `read_local_artifact_content` are untouched.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Verdict | Count |\\n|---|---|\\n| VERIFIED | 7 |\\n| REFUTED | 0 |\\n| INCONCLUSIVE | 0 |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nArtifact writes have no append mode. Every update to a stored artifact is a full-file rewrite:\\n\\n- `store_artifact_content` (`artifact_provider.py:503-537` / `:1053-1091`) calls `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` which replaces the file contents verbatim.\\n- PyGithub's `Gist.edit` is full-file replacement \u2014 verified against `github/Gist.py` and `github/InputFileContent.py` on the `main` branch. `InputFileContent` exposes only `content` and `new_name`; there is no byte-range, offset, or patch-mode parameter.\\n- The underlying GitHub REST API endpoint `PATCH /gists/{gist_id}` also performs full-file replacement \u2014 it accepts `{content: string}` per file and the key \\\"must match the current filename\\\".\\n- grep for `artifact_append` across backlog_core returns zero matches.\\n\\nA producer that wants to write an artifact larger than the 10K-token MCP call ceiling is blocked. Its only option is to read the current content, concatenate in memory, and PATCH the complete new blob \u2014 an O(N\u00b2) cost that also requires the producer to already have read the previous state, which is itself bounded by the same 10K ceiling.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"96db4d1e003b7bcc5a6cf3288111c52330008ce6fc11babde0dbc4a45fce7b59\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS-NRg\"}"}